        "### 3.1 Data quality checks\n",
        "\n",
        "**Table 1. Summary of data quality checks**\n",
        "\n",
        "| Check | Finding | Action taken |\n",
        "|---|---|---|\n",
        "| Missing values | None in either file ✓ | None required |\n",
        "| Missing days | None; both files are continuous daily series ✓ | None required |\n",
        "| Train/test overlap | 2017-01-01 appears in both files ✗ | Removed from the training set |\n",
        "| Final training row (2017-01-01) | Mean temperature drops abruptly to 10 °C and humidity reaches 100%, inconsistent with neighbouring days (Figure 1) ✗ | Resolved by the removal above (same row) |\n",
        "| `meanpressure` range | Train: min −3.04 hPa, max 7679 hPa. Test: min 59 hPa. Realistic range ≈ 950–1050 hPa ✗ | Out-of-range values (9 train, 1 test) replaced by time-based linear interpolation |\n",
        "| `meantemp` range | Train: 6.0–38.7 °C. Test: 11.0–34.5 °C ✓ | None required; test values lie within the training range |"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "# Cleaning the dataset\n",
        "\n",
        "# 1. Remove the overlapping date from the training set\n",
        "# 2017-01-01 appears in both files. The training-file version is anomalous\n",
        "# (sudden temperature drop, humidity = 100%), and keeping it would also let\n",
        "# the test period leak into training. The test-file version is kept.\n",
        "print(\"Training row being removed:\\n\", train_df.loc['2017-01-01'], \"\\n\")\n",
        "train_df = train_df.drop(pd.Timestamp('2017-01-01'))\n",
        "\n",
        "# 2. Clean physically impossible meanpressure values\n",
        "# Realistic sea-level pressure is roughly 950-1050 hPa. Values outside this\n",
        "# range are sensor errors: replace them with NaN, then fill them by\n",
        "# time-based linear interpolation from neighbouring days.\n",
        "P_MIN, P_MAX = 950, 1050\n",
        "\n",
        "def clean_pressure(d, name):\n",
        "    d = d.copy()\n",
        "    bad = (d['meanpressure'] < P_MIN) | (d['meanpressure'] > P_MAX)\n",
        "    print(f\"{name}: {bad.sum()} invalid meanpressure values replaced\")\n",
        "    d.loc[bad, 'meanpressure'] = np.nan\n",
        "    d['meanpressure'] = d['meanpressure'].interpolate(method='time').bfill().ffill()\n",
        "    return d\n",
        "\n",
        "train_df = clean_pressure(train_df, 'Train')\n",
        "test_df  = clean_pressure(test_df,  'Test')\n",
        "\n",
        "# 3. Confirm the result\n",
        "print(f\"\\nTrain: {len(train_df)} rows, {train_df.index.min().date()} to {train_df.index.max().date()}\")\n",
        "print(f\"Test : {len(test_df)} rows, {test_df.index.min().date()} to {test_df.index.max().date()}\")\n",
        "display(train_df.describe().round(2))"
