        "### 3.2 Cleaning decisions\n",
        "- **Train/test overlap:** the training-file entry for 2017-01-01 was removed so that the test set stays completely unseen, and because its values are anomalous. Final sizes: **1461 training days** (2013-01-01 to 2016-12-31) and **114 test days** (2017-01-01 to 2017-04-24).\n",
        "- **Pressure sensor errors:** values outside 950–1050 hPa are physically impossible and were treated as sensor faults (9 training and 1 test value). This does not affect the models, which use only `meantemp`, but keeps the dataset valid.\n",
        "- **Scaling range:** test temperatures lie inside the training range, so a MinMax scaler fitted on training data maps the test data into [0, 1] without extrapolation.\n",
        "- **Seasonality:** `meantemp` has a strong yearly cycle, cold in December–January and hot in May–June (Figure 2). The test period (January–April 2017) is the **warming phase** of this cycle."
      ]
    },
