        "This lab compared an AR model and an LSTM network for one-day-ahead prediction of Delhi's daily mean temperature, using a chronological train/validation/test split, a persistence baseline and controlled hyperparameter tuning. The EDA showed that the series is non-stationary, strongly seasonal and highly persistent (lag-1 PACF 0.972), with short-term dependence within about 4–11 days. This guided the selection of AR(11) and an LSTM with a 7-day window and 16 units.\n",
